7. This Court has considered following aspects,
(i) Applicants - Pooja Hiranandani and Dipti R/CR.MA/8202/2022 ORDER DATED: 20/04/2023 Dharmeshbhai Aashar are the lady applicants / accused who have, pursuant to the interim orders of this Court dated 04.05.2022 and 01.06.2022, appeared before the Investigating Officer and their statements have been recorded and they have already submitted the documents which were there in their custody;
(ii) Prima facie this seems to be a civil dispute relating to accounting between ex-partners and present partners;
(iii) Even as per the report submitted by the Police Inspector, Local Crime Branch, East Kachchh - Gandhidham, the allegations made in the FIR are not substantiated by the material available on record during the course of investigation;
(iv) No antecedents are reported against the applicants.
8.

The applicants are ordered to be released on bail in the event of their arrest in connection with FIR C.R.No.11993006220288 of 2022 registered with A Division, Gandhidham Police Station, Kachchh East - Gandhidham, on executing a personal bond of Rs.10,000/- (Rupees Ten Thousand Only) each with one surety of like amount on the following conditions:
Pooja Chandubhai Hirananadani vs State Of Gujarat on 20 April, 2023 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/170394928/
3 (a) shall cooperate with the investigation and make themselves available for interrogation whenever required;

(c) shall not directly or indirectly make any inducement, threat or promise to any person acquainted with the fact of the case so as to dissuade them from disclosing such facts to the court or to any police officer;
(d) shall not obstruct or hamper the police investigation and not to play mischief with the evidence collected or yet to be collected by the police;
(e) shall at the time of execution of bond, furnish the address to the investigating officer and the court concerned and shall not change residence till the final disposal of the case till further orders;
(f) shall not leave India without the permission of the concerned trial court and if having passport shall deposit the same before the concerned trial court within a week; and R/CR.MA/8202/2022 ORDER DATED: 20/04/2023 (g) it would be open to the Investigating Officer to file an application for remand if they consider it proper and just and the learned Magistrate would decide it on merits;
